meta {
  name: List Objects
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/schema/{{connectionId}}/objects
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~schema: public
  ~kind: procedure
}

docs {
  Procedures, functions, views and triggers in a schema (Postgres/MSSQL; empty for Mongo/ES). Read live, not cached.

  Each entry is { schema, name, kind, args?, parent? }: `args` (Postgres routines) are the identity argument types that tell overloads apart; `parent` is a trigger's table. `kind` filters to one of procedure | function | view | trigger.

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}) plus **read** capability for the connection's environment — 403 otherwise (admins hold every environment).

  Errors: 503 { error, code: "CONNECTION_FAILED" } when the database host is
  unreachable (network); 500 { error } for other introspection failures.
}
